<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">South Asia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> is the region comprising the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-subcontinent">Indian subcontinent</a>, including modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, Bangladesh, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>. It was ruled by empires including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> profile notes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a>'s invasion of the region in 1738–1739.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-asia.jpg" alt="South Asia" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: user:Serg!o · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:South_Asia_(orthographic_projection)_without_national_boundaries.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
